Z||000000||Silver Bullet||08-28-99||11:14 PM||||I was wondering if anybody knew of any really good sites or catalogs that carried good aftermarket performance parts for decent prices.  If u know of any, please don't be greedy!!<br>
Z||000001||DXR_MOM||08-28-99||11:54 PM||||Welcome Aboard Silver Bullet, I live in San Francisco and the prices out here for Fiero parts maybe a slight bit higher, but my suggestion to is to continue to follow the post on this forum and you will receive mounds of information on where to purchase Fiero parts and services.  One tip is to find a good machanic and only go to him.  Since we have owned our Fiero, there is one shop we go to for all repairs and services.  Also, we have done some mods on our own as well.  Getting to know a local machine shop would be a plus as you may need to have part customed made.  So keep posting and all your questions will be answered.  Good Luck
Z||000002||batboy||08-29-99||02:39 AM||||When it comes to general high performance parts, it's hard to beat JEGS, www.jegs.com, although they specialize more in V8 parts, they do have some V6 stuff. Another good source for engine parts is Performance Automotive Warehouse (PAW), but again they carry mostly V8 parts.
